= The Party Is Broken

The district offices are closed and their secretaries in prison, in exile or dead. The membership lists have been seized or burned. Fewer than a thousand people in all of Germany still pay dues to the party, and most of them no longer know whom to pay them to.

Parties have come back from worse, in other countries and other centuries. This one will not, not in this generation.

- @end: See how it ends.

